WEBVTT

00:00.516 --> 00:01.915
&lt;i>Previously on&lt;/i>
Two and a Half Men...

00:02.110 --> 00:03.877
Excuse me, do you know
the difference

00:03.902 --> 00:06.352
between "organic beef"
and "grass-fed beef"?

00:07.039 --> 00:08.238
She was totally hitting on you.

00:08.324 --> 00:09.908
You should ask her out.

00:10.057 --> 00:12.808
Hey, Zoey, you want
to on a date with me?!

00:12.810 --> 00:14.260
Sure!

00:14.262 --> 00:16.879
When I was in high school,
I met this girl named Bridget.

00:16.881 --> 00:18.914
You're still in love
with her, aren't you?

00:18.916 --> 00:20.382
See, look. No wedding ring.

00:20.384 --> 00:22.585
Hmm, I noticed
the bright white tan line.

00:22.587 --> 00:24.386
No worries. I gave it to Alan.

00:24.388 --> 00:27.223
Oh... very valuable.

00:28.843 --> 00:30.676
You seem like
a really sweet guy,

00:30.678 --> 00:34.513
but I think you're still kind
of married to your Bridget.

00:34.515 --> 00:37.650
Face it, you're not ready
to be dating yet.

00:38.768 --> 00:40.969
You want your ring back?

00:40.971 --> 00:42.071
Yeah.

00:42.073 --> 00:43.639
I don't need this anymore.

00:43.641 --> 00:44.907
You sure?

00:44.909 --> 00:47.243
I'm positive.

00:48.311 --> 00:50.613
My precious! My precious!

00:53.500 --> 00:56.151
My precious! My precious!

00:58.288 --> 01:00.623
My precious!

01:05.211 --> 01:07.179
Mind if I take this?

01:07.181 --> 01:09.131
Oh, uh, no--
somebody's sitting there.

01:09.133 --> 01:11.333
Well, where are they?

01:11.335 --> 01:12.635
They're not here yet.

01:12.637 --> 01:14.937
Well, I'm here
and I need a chair.

01:14.939 --> 01:16.639
No, uh...

01:16.641 --> 01:18.774
honestly, I have a girl coming.

01:18.776 --> 01:21.443
Well, when she gets here,
I'll give it back to her.

01:21.445 --> 01:24.697
See, I don't believe that.

01:27.016 --> 01:29.201
You calling me a liar?

01:29.203 --> 01:33.489
No, but I've been burnt before.

01:33.491 --> 01:36.024
I'm taking this chair.

01:36.026 --> 01:37.543
No, you're not.

01:37.545 --> 01:39.912
Yes, I am. Let go!

01:39.914 --> 01:41.246
You let go
of the chair.

01:41.248 --> 01:42.965
I had the chair before
you even came into the place.

01:42.967 --> 01:44.550
- It's mine now!
- It's my chair now!

01:44.552 --> 01:46.468
Walden, is everything all right?

01:46.470 --> 01:48.487
Ha! She's here.
Now back off!

01:50.256 --> 01:51.557
What was that all about?

01:51.559 --> 01:53.559
It was an attempt
at a chairjacking.

01:53.561 --> 01:56.145
Here, I get you a tea.

01:56.147 --> 01:58.430
Thank you.
I'm sorry I'm late.

01:58.432 --> 02:00.733
I'm trying to get my daughter
into Bellwood Academy.

02:00.735 --> 02:02.484
It's a nightmare.

02:02.486 --> 02:05.187
She tests well, but she did
not give a good interview.

02:05.189 --> 02:06.388
How old is
your daughter again?

02:06.390 --> 02:08.023
Five.

02:08.025 --> 02:11.193
And Bellwood Academy is a...?
Kindergarten.

02:11.195 --> 02:14.413
Wow, when I was five,
I got kicked out of preschool

02:14.415 --> 02:15.531
for biting my teacher.

02:15.533 --> 02:16.865
Why did you bite her?

02:16.867 --> 02:18.751
She tried to steal my chair.

02:20.403 --> 02:22.070
Yeah, you heard me! I bit her!

02:23.506 --> 02:24.906
She had to get a shot!

02:27.010 --> 02:28.677
Take it easy, okay?

02:29.929 --> 02:31.380
So I was rather surprised

02:31.382 --> 02:32.881
to hear from you.
What's up?

02:32.883 --> 02:35.968
I was thinking a lot about what
you said about not wanting

02:35.970 --> 02:39.421
to date me while I was
still, you know,

02:39.423 --> 02:41.089
emotionally attached
to my ex-wife.

02:41.091 --> 02:44.026
I said you were still
hopelessly in love with her.

02:44.028 --> 02:46.729
Potato, Po-tah-to.

02:46.731 --> 02:48.263
The point is you were right.

02:48.265 --> 02:50.482
I wasn't ready to start
dating, but I am now.

02:50.484 --> 02:53.235
A whole week later.

02:53.237 --> 02:55.037
I understand your skepticism.

02:55.039 --> 02:57.906
Which is why I want you to
witness what I'm about to do.

02:57.908 --> 02:59.875
These...

02:59.877 --> 03:02.294
are my final divorce papers.

03:03.413 --> 03:07.383
And once I sign them, my
marriage will be over forever.

03:08.585 --> 03:11.637
I was hoping that you
and I could start fresh.

03:11.639 --> 03:14.673
Nothing like starting off
a new relationship

03:14.675 --> 03:16.458
on the ashes of the old one.

03:16.460 --> 03:18.960
That's what I was thinking.

03:21.798 --> 03:23.315
Oh, uh, you got a pen?

03:23.317 --> 03:25.734
Uh, I don't think I do.

03:25.736 --> 03:26.802
Okay.

03:26.804 --> 03:29.137
Uh, does anybody got a pen
I can borrow?

03:30.156 --> 03:32.140
Anyone? Nobody?

03:32.142 --> 03:33.141
Excuse me.

03:33.143 --> 03:34.076
Do you got a pen?

03:34.078 --> 03:35.143
Sorry.

03:35.145 --> 03:38.113
It's unbelievable.

03:41.000 --> 03:43.985
Oh, man.

03:43.987 --> 03:46.088
Can I please borrow your pen?

03:46.090 --> 03:49.675
I'm sorry, someone's using it.

03:49.677 --> 03:50.959
Who?

03:50.961 --> 03:53.479
They're not here yet.

03:54.781 --> 03:57.666
I will give you a hundred
dollars to borrow that pen.

04:01.187 --> 04:04.106
♪ Men, men, men, men, manly men,
men, men ♪

04:04.108 --> 04:07.175
♪ Men, men, manly men, men, men ♪
♪ Ooh ♪

04:07.177 --> 04:10.529
♪ Men, men, men, men, manly men ♪
♪ Ooh ♪

04:10.531 --> 04:12.815
♪ Ooh-ooh-ooh,
ooh-ohh, ooh-ooh... ♪

04:12.817 --> 04:15.284
♪ Men, men, men, men, manly men,
men, men ♪

04:15.286 --> 04:18.620
♪ Ooh ♪
♪ Men, men, men, manly men, men, men ♪

04:18.622 --> 04:22.207
♪ Ah. ♪
♪ Men. ♪

04:22.232 --> 04:26.232
&lt;font color="#00FF00">♪ Two and a Half Men 9x11 ♪&lt;/font>
&lt;font color="#00FFFF">What a Lovely Landing Strip&lt;/font>
Original Air Date on December 21, 2011

04:26.257 --> 04:30.257
== sync, corrected by &lt;font color="#00FF00">elderman&lt;/font> ==

04:32.533 --> 04:36.336
Jolly good sunset, eh, what?

04:36.338 --> 04:38.371
Excuse me?

04:38.373 --> 04:39.872
I like the way you talk,

04:39.874 --> 04:42.708
so I thought
I'd give it a go.

04:42.710 --> 04:45.428
Well, no one says "jolly good"
unless they're appearing in

04:45.430 --> 04:47.213
a revival of &lt;i>Oliver.&lt;/i>

04:47.215 --> 04:50.733
Right, right, right, right,
right, right.

04:50.735 --> 04:52.819
Please, sir,
may I have a kiss?

04:52.821 --> 04:54.821
Stop it!

04:54.823 --> 04:57.056
No, seriously, I want a kiss.

04:58.409 --> 04:59.659
All right.

05:01.912 --> 05:05.331
- Mm. So...
- Hmm?

05:05.333 --> 05:07.083
would you like to stay
for dinner tonight?

05:07.085 --> 05:09.669
Oh, I'd love to, but I have
to pick up my daughter.

05:09.671 --> 05:10.736
- Yeah?
- Mm-hmm.

05:10.738 --> 05:13.173
- How about dinner this weekend?
- Sure.

05:13.175 --> 05:15.708
Great.
You like Mexican food?

05:15.710 --> 05:17.076
I do.

05:17.078 --> 05:18.511
Ooh, terrific.

05:18.513 --> 05:20.096
So we'll go to Guadalajara.

05:20.098 --> 05:21.965
Oh, that a new
restaurant?

05:21.967 --> 05:24.267
No, it's an old city in Mexico.

05:24.269 --> 05:26.970
You want to go to
Mexico for dinner?

05:26.972 --> 05:29.472
Yep. We'll take my plane.

05:29.474 --> 05:30.807
I'll have you back
by midnight.

05:30.809 --> 05:33.059
So, hang on--
you-you don't own a pen,

05:33.061 --> 05:34.727
but you own a plane?

05:34.729 --> 05:36.262
Yeah, you can
always borrow a pen.

05:36.264 --> 05:37.597
Try to borrow a plane.

05:38.949 --> 05:40.149
- So...
- Mm?

05:40.151 --> 05:41.484
what do you say?

05:41.486 --> 05:45.455
Hmm... Let me see if
I can get a sitter.

05:45.457 --> 05:46.906
Oh!

05:46.908 --> 05:47.991
Yay!

05:47.993 --> 05:49.792
- Mm-hmm.
- You know, I think we should

05:49.794 --> 05:51.944
start making plans
for Christmas.

05:51.946 --> 05:56.049
We can go surfing in Fiji,
skiing in the Alps,

05:56.051 --> 05:57.066
making out in Malibu.

05:57.068 --> 05:59.836
Yes, now, Walden,
let's be very clear:

05:59.838 --> 06:02.305
You are a sweet and
wonderful guy,

06:02.307 --> 06:03.590
but you've just come out

06:03.592 --> 06:05.791
of a very long-term relationship,
- Sweet and wonderful.

06:05.793 --> 06:07.627
so you're clearly on
the rebound.

06:07.629 --> 06:09.178
Uh-huh. So?

06:09.180 --> 06:10.346
Yes. So I don't know

06:10.348 --> 06:12.932
if we should be making
Christmas plans just yet.

06:12.934 --> 06:14.317
- Okay.
- Hmm?

06:14.319 --> 06:17.904
Fine.
We'll slow things down.

06:17.906 --> 06:18.988
Good.

06:18.990 --> 06:20.156
Forget Christmas.

06:20.158 --> 06:21.824
Thank you.

06:21.826 --> 06:23.359
You'll be my Valentine,
though, right?

06:23.361 --> 06:24.410
Oh, my God.

06:24.412 --> 06:27.030
You're like no man
I've ever met.

06:27.032 --> 06:28.665
Mmm! A bit of an
odd bloke, eh, what?

06:28.667 --> 06:29.832
Oh, God, stop it.

06:29.834 --> 06:31.784
Nudge, nudge, wink, wink,
say no more.

06:35.256 --> 06:38.057
This is nice.
Like old times.

06:38.059 --> 06:39.042
How so?

06:39.044 --> 06:41.361
You and me, sitting
here, watching TV

06:41.363 --> 06:43.162
while the good-looking
owner of the house is

06:43.164 --> 06:45.965
out on the deck swapping
spit with a hot chick.

06:45.967 --> 06:49.602
Yeah, there is
a bit of deja vu.

06:49.604 --> 06:50.637
Not only that.

06:50.639 --> 06:53.006
It feels like it's
happened before.

06:56.060 --> 06:57.977
Yes, it does.

06:59.697 --> 07:02.482
Man, I've seen so much
crazy stuff in this house,

07:02.484 --> 07:03.700
I could write a book.

07:03.702 --> 07:05.752
That's a good idea.
Got a title?

07:05.754 --> 07:07.403
Hmm...

07:07.405 --> 07:08.871
Maybe I can't
write a book.

07:08.873 --> 07:11.441
All right then, cheerio!

07:12.494 --> 07:13.710
Cheerio?

07:13.712 --> 07:15.328
Means "good-bye"
in England.

07:15.330 --> 07:16.462
Oh.

07:16.464 --> 07:17.997
What do they have for
breakfast over there,

07:17.999 --> 07:19.832
a bowl of good-byes?

07:21.151 --> 07:22.835
- 'Ello, lads.
- Well, hey.

07:22.837 --> 07:25.338
So, Zoey seems very nice.

07:25.340 --> 07:28.708
Yeah, the bird really tickles
my fancy.

07:28.710 --> 07:30.009
Help me out here.

07:30.011 --> 07:32.545
Is "fancy" the English
word for "nutsack"?

07:35.849 --> 07:38.017
No, it means that I like her.

07:38.019 --> 07:39.769
I think this could get serious.

07:39.771 --> 07:41.821
Wow, you're moving pretty quick,
aren't you?

07:41.823 --> 07:43.656
That's what she said.

07:44.826 --> 07:46.492
What are you laughing at?

07:46.494 --> 07:48.561
He did a "That's what
she said" joke.

07:48.563 --> 07:49.746
Because that's what she said.

07:49.748 --> 07:54.033
Oh. That's not funny.

07:54.035 --> 07:56.369
She thinks I'm on the rebound.

07:56.371 --> 07:57.737
Well, aren't you?

07:57.739 --> 07:59.455
You were with Bridget
for 15 years.

07:59.457 --> 08:01.874
That's over.
I signed the divorce papers.

08:01.876 --> 08:04.844
I'm ready to fall in love again.

08:04.846 --> 08:07.847
Please tell me you didn't
actually say that to her.

08:07.849 --> 08:08.931
Why?

08:08.933 --> 08:12.218
Dude, even I know that's wrong.

08:14.271 --> 08:16.556
Walden, you're young,
you're rich, you're handsome.

08:16.558 --> 08:18.358
If I was even one
of those things

08:18.360 --> 08:21.027
I would have screwed myself
to death years ago.

08:21.029 --> 08:23.095
Well, I want to be in
a relationship...

08:23.097 --> 08:27.033
with romance and intimacy
and commitment.

08:27.035 --> 08:29.602
Oh, I get it. You're a chick.

08:31.739 --> 08:34.106
Jake, we're living in
his house.

08:34.108 --> 08:37.126
A very nice chick.

08:44.968 --> 08:48.337
This is absolutely
ridiculous.

08:48.339 --> 08:50.673
You don't have to wear the hat
if you don't want to.

08:50.675 --> 08:53.976
It's not the hat.
Well, it's not totally the hat.

08:53.978 --> 08:57.764
It's the incredible
extravagance.

08:57.766 --> 09:00.733
You do realize I'm still not
ready to sleep with you, yes?

09:00.735 --> 09:02.301
Oh, I'm not trying
to have sex with you.

09:02.303 --> 09:04.570
Why not?
What's wrong with me?

09:04.572 --> 09:07.273
Nothing. Why? Do you want
to have sex with me?

09:07.275 --> 09:10.660
Yeah! No! No, it's too soon.
It's too soon.

09:10.662 --> 09:13.780
Well, is it too soon...

09:13.782 --> 09:15.531
for this?

09:15.533 --> 09:18.618
Oh, God, Walden,
what have you done?

09:24.675 --> 09:25.792
What do you think?

09:25.794 --> 09:28.344
I think you're out
of your bloody mind.

09:28.346 --> 09:29.679
I can't accept this.

09:29.681 --> 09:30.663
Why not?

09:30.665 --> 09:32.849
Because it's too much.

09:32.851 --> 09:34.517
It's crazy!

09:34.519 --> 09:36.769
What about getting a diamond
necklace for a girl

09:36.771 --> 09:37.887
you've haven't slept with yet

09:37.889 --> 09:39.355
while flying to Mexico
for dinner

09:39.357 --> 09:41.274
on your private jet is crazy?

09:42.309 --> 09:44.060
Okay, when I say it out loud

09:44.062 --> 09:45.478
it does sound a little crazy.

09:45.480 --> 09:48.030
Good thing I didn't get you
the matching tiara.

09:49.182 --> 09:51.984
Okay, uh, there might be
one other thing.

09:51.986 --> 09:54.454
Oh, God, you didn't buy me
a pony, did you?

09:54.456 --> 09:55.855
No. Why, do you want one?

09:55.857 --> 09:56.856
No, I don't.

09:56.858 --> 09:59.692
The thing is, I know some people

09:59.694 --> 10:01.461
on the board
of the private school

10:01.463 --> 10:03.663
you're trying to get
your daughter in,

10:03.665 --> 10:05.331
so I pulled some strings
and got her enrolled.

10:05.333 --> 10:09.001
Wait-- you got Ava
into Bellwood?

10:09.003 --> 10:12.004
But don't worry, one phone call
and she's out on her ass.

10:12.006 --> 10:13.873
No, don't do that!

10:13.875 --> 10:15.207
Walden, this is wonderful!

10:15.209 --> 10:17.209
You're not upset?

10:17.211 --> 10:19.846
No! No, no, no.

10:19.848 --> 10:21.848
What you did is brilliant.

10:21.850 --> 10:24.350
Mm!
Utterly brilliant.

10:24.352 --> 10:27.153
Mr. Schmidt, we'll be descending

10:27.155 --> 10:30.573
into Guadalajara in
a few minutes.

10:30.575 --> 10:33.025
Circle, circle!

10:33.027 --> 10:35.244
Excuse me?

10:35.246 --> 10:39.398
He's about to descend
into London.

10:42.286 --> 10:45.004
&lt;i>Hello, Heathrow!&lt;/i>

10:45.006 --> 10:46.839
Oh, God, that is
&lt;i>not funny.&lt;/i>

10:46.841 --> 10:50.626
&lt;i>What a lovely&lt;/i>
&lt;i>landing strip.&lt;/i>

10:50.628 --> 10:53.462
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

10:53.931 --> 10:55.882
- Morning.
- Morning.

10:57.935 --> 11:00.803
Want to explain
the hat?

11:00.805 --> 11:02.605
It's not a hat, it's a sombrero.

11:02.607 --> 11:05.257
"Sombrero" is Spanish for "hat""

11:05.259 --> 11:07.026
Really?
Seems awfully complicated.

11:07.028 --> 11:08.928
Why don't they
just call it a hat?

11:11.765 --> 11:13.766
No, not worth it.

11:13.768 --> 11:15.701
- Morning.
- Morning.

11:15.703 --> 11:17.102
Cameron Diaz, señor.

11:19.489 --> 11:21.290
- Cameron Diaz?
- Choose your battles.

11:21.292 --> 11:23.242
Right.

11:23.244 --> 11:25.077
So, how'd it go last night?

11:25.079 --> 11:26.495
It was great.

11:26.497 --> 11:27.663
I think I'm falling in love.

11:27.665 --> 11:31.116
Oh, Walden, that's
muy grande chiquita.

11:32.252 --> 11:34.587
Hey, man...

11:34.589 --> 11:36.622
I really don't appreciate
you making fun of me.

11:36.624 --> 11:37.974
Sorry.

11:40.228 --> 11:43.312
I'll get it.

11:45.232 --> 11:47.149
Who knew he spoke Spanish?

11:49.019 --> 11:53.806
♪ Zoey, Zoey,
Zoey, Zoe, Zoey... ♪

11:53.808 --> 11:55.441
Bridget.

11:55.443 --> 11:57.360
I can't sign the divorce papers.

11:57.362 --> 11:59.528
I love you and I want you back.

12:01.448 --> 12:03.499
Oh, bollocks.

12:03.501 --> 12:05.150
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

12:09.067 --> 12:11.485
Wait... whoa, whoa,
wait, I...

12:11.487 --> 12:12.653
I don't understand.

12:12.655 --> 12:14.255
You're the one who
wanted the divorce.

12:14.257 --> 12:15.656
I know-- I thought
it's what I wanted,

12:15.658 --> 12:17.041
but when I saw your name
on the papers,

12:17.043 --> 12:19.143
I just, I couldn't sign.

12:19.145 --> 12:20.661
Ay, Chihuahua.

12:20.663 --> 12:22.062
Stop it.

12:22.064 --> 12:24.865
Sorry, it's the hat.

12:24.867 --> 12:27.501
Is everything okay?
You don't look happy.

12:27.503 --> 12:28.736
Yeah, no, yeah,
it's great.

12:28.738 --> 12:29.920
I just...

12:29.922 --> 12:31.494
What about that doctor
you were dating?

12:31.519 --> 12:32.407
Alex?

12:32.408 --> 12:34.875
I saw him.
He's a dreamboat.

12:34.877 --> 12:37.211
The truth is, he was
just a rebound thing.

12:37.213 --> 12:39.547
Yeah, but rebounds
work out sometimes.

12:39.549 --> 12:40.748
I mean, take Abe Lincoln.

12:40.750 --> 12:42.133
He met his wife on a rebound,

12:42.135 --> 12:44.552
and, and they had a
long-term relationship.

12:44.554 --> 12:46.420
Until, you know...

12:48.440 --> 12:51.726
Hm... I didn't know
Abe Lincoln killed himself.

12:53.562 --> 12:56.597
How many rebounds have you
had since we broke up?

12:56.599 --> 12:57.915
Well...

12:57.917 --> 12:59.183
It's a trap, don't answer.

12:59.185 --> 13:01.285
None that meant anything.

13:01.287 --> 13:02.436
Yes!

13:02.438 --> 13:03.937
I mean, I haven't
exactly been celibate.

13:03.939 --> 13:05.773
- Oh, no, no, no, no, no!
- But I haven't been a slut, either.

13:05.775 --> 13:07.124
Attaboy.

13:07.126 --> 13:10.378
Come on, let's go upstairs.

13:10.380 --> 13:12.630
- Really?
- Don't you want to?

13:12.632 --> 13:14.799
Well, yeah, I want to.

13:14.801 --> 13:17.752
I just, I-I...shouldn't
we be taking it slow?

13:17.754 --> 13:20.054
We've been married
for 15 years, Walden.

13:20.056 --> 13:21.272
Come on.

13:21.274 --> 13:23.391
Okay.

13:23.393 --> 13:25.626
- Hello.
- Hey.

13:25.628 --> 13:27.895
Hi.

13:27.897 --> 13:31.599
It's very weird that you
live with these people.

13:33.352 --> 13:35.903
So what's he gonna
do about Zoey?

13:35.905 --> 13:38.689
Well, unless I miss my guess,

13:38.691 --> 13:42.326
he's gonna lie to both of them
until it blows up in his face,

13:42.328 --> 13:44.362
and everyone gets
their feelings hurt,

13:44.364 --> 13:46.330
and he's left alone
and miserable.

13:46.332 --> 13:48.249
Wow. That sucks.
Isn't there a better way to

13:48.251 --> 13:51.085
date two women
at the same time?

13:51.087 --> 13:53.037
Aw, Jake...

13:53.039 --> 13:55.989
No.

13:55.991 --> 13:59.343
I want you so badly.

13:59.345 --> 14:01.712
Yeah, yep, I, uh...

14:01.714 --> 14:04.465
...want you too.
I was such a fool.

14:04.467 --> 14:06.500
I can't believe I let someone
as great as you get away.

14:06.502 --> 14:08.302
Wait, you said I was immature.

14:08.304 --> 14:10.838
You are, but that's
part of your charm.

14:10.840 --> 14:12.940
I love you, Walden.

14:12.942 --> 14:17.194
I love you, I love you,
I love you.

14:17.196 --> 14:19.196
That is awesome.

14:19.198 --> 14:20.147
Uh...

14:20.149 --> 14:23.150
Just... okay,
okay, well...

14:23.152 --> 14:25.453
Can we just hold on
for one second?

14:25.455 --> 14:28.205
- Where are you going?
- Uh, the bathroom.

14:28.207 --> 14:29.857
Why don't you just use that one?

14:29.859 --> 14:32.025
I'm a little pee shy.

14:32.027 --> 14:33.694
I don't want you to hear me.

14:33.696 --> 14:34.962
Since when?

14:34.964 --> 14:36.380
It's a new thing.

14:36.382 --> 14:37.882
People change, Bridget,
people grow.

14:39.200 --> 14:43.037
Do you think you and Mom
would ever get back together?

14:43.039 --> 14:46.206
Well, you know I will always
care for your mother.

14:46.208 --> 14:49.393
She's a terrific lady,
and a great mom,

14:49.395 --> 14:52.713
and no one can predict
the future...

14:52.715 --> 14:54.732
but no freakin' way.

14:54.734 --> 14:56.884
She said the same thing.

14:56.886 --> 15:00.387
But used a different word
than "freakin'."

15:00.389 --> 15:01.405
- Hey.
- Hey.

15:01.407 --> 15:03.190
Hey.

15:03.192 --> 15:04.525
Everything all right?

15:04.527 --> 15:06.360
Uh, no. As Zoey would say,

15:06.362 --> 15:08.412
I'm in a bit of a sticky wicket.

15:08.414 --> 15:10.397
You mean you were
in a sticky wicket,

15:10.399 --> 15:12.900
then you finished up and
came down here for a snack.

15:12.902 --> 15:17.271
No, no, I-I have a conundrum.

15:17.273 --> 15:18.589
Then you should've worn it.

15:18.591 --> 15:21.926
Might've avoided the stickiness,
you know, wicket-wise.

15:23.428 --> 15:25.224
Okay, I'm just going
to talk to you.

15:25.249 --> 15:26.348
Please.

15:26.349 --> 15:28.516
I've been dreaming about getting
back together with Bridget

15:28.518 --> 15:32.920
for months now, but since
I met Zoey, I'm not so sure.

15:32.922 --> 15:34.738
- It is a pickle.
- What's a pickle?

15:34.740 --> 15:37.191
Shh.

15:37.193 --> 15:38.592
What does your heart tell you?

15:38.594 --> 15:41.479
My heart tells me that

15:41.481 --> 15:44.114
Bridget is the past,
and Zoey is the future.

15:44.116 --> 15:46.033
Oh, I get it.
You're trying to figure out

15:46.035 --> 15:47.284
which one gets your pickle.

15:48.403 --> 15:49.954
Essentially, yes.

15:49.956 --> 15:53.040
Well, then, I say
follow your heart.

15:53.042 --> 15:54.375
I say follow your pickle.

15:56.211 --> 15:57.878
Try to ignore him.

15:57.880 --> 16:00.714
I've been with Bridget
for 15 years.

16:00.716 --> 16:02.132
That's tough to
just walk away from.

16:02.134 --> 16:03.951
But as you said yourself,
Bridget's the past.

16:03.953 --> 16:05.803
Yeah, but if I get
back together with her,

16:05.805 --> 16:07.505
I don't have to
give up $600 million

16:07.507 --> 16:08.589
in a divorce settlement.

16:08.591 --> 16:10.424
The future's overrated.
Go with Bridget.

16:10.426 --> 16:12.676
I mean, it does make sense,
right? All I'd have to do

16:12.678 --> 16:14.228
is sell this place
and move back in with her.

16:14.230 --> 16:15.846
You can't live your
life in the past.

16:15.848 --> 16:17.815
- Go with Zoey.
- You think?

16:17.817 --> 16:19.817
I do. And I don't have
a horse in this race.

16:19.819 --> 16:21.468
No, you're right.

16:21.470 --> 16:22.820
Zoey it is.

16:22.822 --> 16:24.304
Thank you, Alan.

16:24.306 --> 16:25.656
Cheerios!

16:28.243 --> 16:30.778
You have no shame, do you?

16:30.780 --> 16:32.363
Shame, no.

16:32.365 --> 16:34.498
Malibu beach house, yes.

16:37.986 --> 16:40.704
Welcome back.

16:40.706 --> 16:43.290
Oh, boy.

16:45.427 --> 16:47.327
Bridget, I can't remember--

16:47.329 --> 16:50.130
do you like your Band-Aids
taken off quick or slow?

16:50.132 --> 16:51.765
I don't understand.

16:51.767 --> 16:54.134
Let's just go with quick.

16:54.136 --> 16:56.670
I don't think it's a good
idea to sleep with you,

16:56.672 --> 16:57.888
since I started
seeing someone new

16:57.890 --> 16:59.807
and I think she might
be the real deal.

16:59.809 --> 17:02.309
Not that you weren't
the real deal,

17:02.311 --> 17:03.677
you're just the ex-real deal,

17:03.679 --> 17:06.346
and she's the next real deal.

17:07.566 --> 17:10.117
Anyway, I'd like for you you to
sign the divorce papers,

17:10.119 --> 17:12.703
so we can both go meet
people we like better.

17:13.989 --> 17:16.540
- What?
- Friends?

17:17.709 --> 17:19.994
- I am so humiliated!
- I'm sorry!

17:19.996 --> 17:22.580
I can't believe you waited till
I was half naked in your bed

17:22.582 --> 17:24.131
to tell me you were
seeing someone else!

17:24.133 --> 17:27.134
Kind of hard to bring up while
you're taking off my pants.

17:28.470 --> 17:29.887
And by the way,
you look sensational.

17:29.889 --> 17:31.371
The Pilates is
really paying off.

17:31.373 --> 17:33.891
Go to hell,
you son of a bitch!

17:33.893 --> 17:35.392
How about an "attaboy" for not

17:35.394 --> 17:37.595
having sex with you out of
respect for the other woman

17:37.597 --> 17:38.679
I'm falling in love with?

17:38.681 --> 17:39.897
Drop dead!

17:45.270 --> 17:47.187
How many times have
we seen this movie?

17:47.189 --> 17:48.555
Too many to count.

17:48.557 --> 17:50.774
Maybe it's the house.

17:50.776 --> 17:52.660
- What do you mean?
- I think it's haunted.

17:52.662 --> 17:56.280
Like, built on an angry
woman burial ground.

17:56.282 --> 17:58.732
Certainly can't be the fault
of the men who live in it.

17:58.734 --> 18:00.501
Sometimes at night,
if I'm really quiet,

18:00.503 --> 18:02.770
I think I can hear
them bitching.

18:07.792 --> 18:10.094
That didn't go as well
as I'd hoped.

18:10.096 --> 18:11.428
I wouldn't worry about it.

18:11.430 --> 18:13.514
She doesn't look like
the type to carry a grudge.

18:22.724 --> 18:25.926
But I don't know her
like you do.

18:26.311 --> 18:28.529
Haunted...

18:29.364 --> 18:32.149
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

18:34.560 --> 18:36.344
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

18:36.346 --> 18:39.847
So the madam
of the brothel opens the door

18:39.849 --> 18:44.235
and there's a man on the stoop
with no arms and no legs.

18:44.237 --> 18:47.655
And she says, "What do you think
you're going to do here?"

18:47.657 --> 18:51.192
And he says,
"I rang the bell, didn't I?"

18:52.912 --> 18:55.079
You're terrible.

18:58.400 --> 19:01.035
Did he break your heart?

19:03.738 --> 19:04.755
Who are you?

19:04.757 --> 19:06.240
That doesn't matter.

19:06.242 --> 19:09.677
Do you want him back, or
do you want him to suffer?

19:11.580 --> 19:13.047
I don't know.

19:13.049 --> 19:14.715
That's all right.

19:14.717 --> 19:16.884
Oftentimes,
they're the same thing.

19:18.570 --> 19:20.888
Come with me,
and I'll teach you.

19:27.529 --> 19:31.529
== sync, corrected by &lt;font color="#00FF00">elderman&lt;/font> ==
